AuthorDate: Tue Mar 11 09:48:05 2025 +0100
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Tue Mar 11 09:48:05 2025 +0100

    Bug 1953353 - Unify coding patterns in browser tests. r=mkmelin

    Our browser extension tests have evolved and certain patterns have been
    established over time, but not all tests have been updated. Most new
    tests are created by copying an older test, which bleeds old patterns
    into new tests.

    This patch unifies our browser tests:
    * use strict mode
    * use `add_setup()` to define the test environment
    * reduce code in global scope and move it into `add_setup()` (for example calls to `registerCleanupFunction()`)
    * use `var` to declare/import system modules
    * use `const` or `let` for global functions and use the `g` prefix (or all caps)
    * use gDefault prefix for global tabmail, about3pane and messagepane variables, to better indicate that they refer to the default window, and not to the current one
    * add licence header to all files
    * always use helper functions for basic account operations

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D241174

